{"r":"Hvv","lane":{"p":511,"e":[{"h":"حَثَّهُ","t":["aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"حَثٌّ"],", ",[1,"He hastened him,"]," or ",[1,"hurried him uninterruptedly,"]," or ",[1,"in any manner."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"حَثَّهُ عَلَيْهِ"],", (S, A, Msb, K,) aor. , (Msb,) inf. n. ",[2,"حَثٌّ"],", (S, Msb, K,) with which are syn. ↓ ",[2,"حُثْحُوثٌ"]," [app. a quasi-inf. n.] and ↓ ",[2,"حِثِّيثَى"]," [an intensive inf. n.]; and ↓ ",[2,"استحثّهُ"],"; and ↓ ",[2,"حثّثهُ"],", (S, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَحْثِيتٌ"],"; (S;) and ↓ ",[2,"احتثّهُ"],"; (A, K;) and ↓ ",[2,"احثّهُ"],"; (K;) and ↓ ",[2,"حَثْحَثَهُ"],"; (S, A, K;) ",[1,"He incited, excited, urged,"]," or ",[1,"instigated, him to it,"]," or ",[1,"to do it,"]," (S, A, Msb, K,) namely, a thing; (S, Msb;) syn. ",[2,"حَرَّضَهُ"],"; (Msb;) or ",[2,"حَضَّهُ"],"; (S, A, K;) or ",[2,"حَثَّ"]," is used in relation to pace, or journeying, or marching; and ",[2,"حَضَّ"]," in other cases: so says El-Hareeree, on the authority of Kh. (TA.) You say, ",[2,"حَثّ دَابّتَهُ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"حَثْحَثَهَا"],", [",[1,"He incited,"]," or ",[1,"urged, his beast,"],"] ",[2,"بِالسَّوْطِ"]," [",[1,"with the whip"],"]. (A.) And ",[2,"حَثَّ الفَرَسَ عَلَى العَدْوِ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"استحثّهُ"],", ",[1,"He made the horse to go quickly,"]," or ",[1,"in a brisk"]," or ",[1,"sprightly manner;"]," or ",[1,"urged him to run by striking him with the foot,"]," or ",[1,"by beating him."]," (Msb.) ― -b2- See also R. Q. 1."],"f":"1"},{"h":"حَثَّ3َ","t":["see 1."],"f":"2"},{"h":"أَحْثَ3َ","t":["see 1."],"f":"4"},{"h":"تحاثّوا","t":["(S, A,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَحَاثٌّ"],", (K,) ",[1,"They incited, excited, urged,"]," or ",[1,"instigated, one another."]," (K, TA.) You say, ",[2,"لَا يَتَحَاثَّونَ عَلَى طَعَامِ المِسْكيِنِ"],[1,"They do not incite, excite, urge,"]," or ",[1,"instigate, one another to feed the needy."]," (S, TA.) And ",[2,"التَّقْوَى أَصْلُ مَا تَحَاثُّ النَّاسُ عَلَيْهِ"]," [",[1,"Piety is the principal,"]," or ",[1,"best, thing to which men incite one another."],"] (A, TA.)"],"f":"6"},{"h":"احتثّ","t":[[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, incited, excited, urged,"]," or ",[1,"instigated."]," (S, K.) -A2- See also 1. This verb is both trans. and intrans. (K.)"],"f":"8"},{"h":"إِسْتَحْثَ3َ","t":["see 1, in two places."],"f":"10"},{"h":"حَثْحَثَ","t":[": see 1, in two places. ― -b2- Also ",[1,"He moved about"]," [a thing]; or ",[1,"put"]," [it] ",[1,"in motion,"]," or ",[1,"into a state of commotion;"]," (K;) [and so ↓ ",[2,"حَثَّ"],", as is implied in the M, voce ",[2,"فَدَّ"],", where it is used as meaning ",[1,"it"]," (a bird) ",[1,"moved,"]," or ",[1,"flapped,"]," its wings.] You say, ",[2,"حَثْحَثَ المِيلَ فِى العَيْنِ"],[1,"He moved about the collyrium-style in the eye."]," (A, TA.) And [hence,] ",[2,"حَثْحَثُوا ذٰلِكَ الأَمْرَ ثُمَّ تَرَكُوهُ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"They stirred up"]," (",[2,"حَرَّكُوا"],") ",[1,"that affair, and then left it,"]," or ",[1,"abandoned it."]," (TA.) ― -b3- ",[1,"He scattered about"]," the utensils, or furniture, of his house, or tent; as also ",[2,"عَثْعَثَ"],". (TA in art. ",[2,"عث"],".) -A2- Also, inf. n. ",[2,"حَثْحَثَةٌ"],", ",[1,"It was,"]," or ",[1,"became, in a state of commotion:"]," (L:) or ",[1,"in a state of consecutive motion."]," (TA.) ",[1,"It"]," (lightning) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, in a state of commotion,"]," (K, TA,) as some say, (TA,) ",[1,"in the clouds."]," (K, TA.) ― -b2- ",[1,"It"]," (rain, and hail, and snow,) ",[1,"appeared and went away, without pouring down."]," (L.) -A3- ",[1,"He"]," (a man) ",[1,"slept."]," (TA.)"],"f":"R. Q. 1"},{"h":"حُثٌّ","t":[[1,"Small particles of straw."]," (S, K, TA.) ― -b2- ",[1,"Anything bruised, brayed,"]," or ",[1,"broken into small particles."]," (L.) ― -b3- ",[1,"Coarse sand:"]," (As, S:) or ",[1,"what is"],[2,"مُتَرَقْرِق"],", (K,) probably, [says SM,] a mistake for ",[2,"مَدْقُوق"]," [",[1,"broken into small particles"],"], agreeably with an explanation of ",[2,"حُثٌّ"]," in the L, for, as to ",[2,"مترقرق"],", [he adds,] I have no